.Dd September 30, 2026
.Dt KVM-WIN 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm kvm-win
.Nd build Windows golden images unattended, and make Windows virtual machines as instant ZFS clones of them
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Cm golden
.Cm win11 | server
.Op Fl -iso Ar url | path
.Op Fl -ram Ar mb
.Op Fl -disk Ar gb
.Nm
.Cm create
.Ar name
.Fl -os Cm win11 | server
.Op Fl -ram Ar mb
.Op Fl -cpus Ar n
.Nm
.Cm list
.Nm
.Cm destroy
.Ar name
.Op Fl -purge
.Nm
.Cm demo sccm
.Nm
.Fl -self-test
.Nm
.Fl h | -help
.Sh DESCRIPTION
Nothing of Windows ships in the kldload image.
.Nm
fetches the media only when a golden is built: Microsoft's evaluation
ISO, found with Mido, or your own with
.Fl -iso ,
and the virtio drivers.
It installs Windows with no one at the console, with the virtio storage
driver loaded before setup, the QEMU guest agent and Cloudbase-Init
added, generalises it with sysprep, and keeps the result as a ZFS volume,
.Ar pool Ns Pa /win- Ns Ar os Ns Pa -golden@golden .
.Pp
Every machine made from it is an instant clone of that snapshot, on q35
with UEFI Secure Boot, a TPM 2.0 and virtio devices \(em what Windows 11
requires.
Cloudbase-Init reads the same NoCloud seed that klab's Linux machines
use, so host name, administrator password, network and first-run commands
are set the cloud-init way.
The administrator is
.Ql Administrator ,
password
.Ql kldload .
.Pp
.Nm
touches only what it made: every clone carries the ZFS property
.Ql com.kldload:kvm-win ,
and
.Cm create
and
.Cm destroy Fl -purge
refuse a volume without it.
.Sh COMMANDS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Cm golden Cm win11 | server
Build the golden, unless it exists.
.Fl -iso
takes your own installation media, a path or a URL; the evaluation
download depends on Microsoft's site and is the less reliable way.
.It Cm create Ar name Fl -os Ar os
Clone the golden and start the machine.
.Ar name
must do as a host name; a volume of that name that
.Nm
did not make is refused.
.It Cm list
The goldens, and every machine
.Nm
made, with its state.
.It Cm destroy Ar name Op Fl -purge
Stop and remove the machine; with
.Fl -purge ,
its volume too.
.It Cm demo sccm
Build both goldens and make a Windows Server and a Windows 11 machine on
the same network, for a configuration-manager demonstration.
.It Fl -self-test
Check the prerequisites \(em virt-install, swtpm, Secure Boot firmware,
ZFS, the libvirt network \(em that the driver download answers, and that
the unattended-setup files are well formed.
.El
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ev KVMWIN_POOL
The dataset holding goldens and clones; default
.Ql rpool/vms .
.It Ev KVMWIN_ISO_DIR , Ev KVMWIN_WORK , Ev KVMWIN_NET
Where media is kept
.Pq Pa /var/lib/libvirt/isos ,
its scratch directory
.Pq Pa /var/lib/kldload/kvm-win ,
and the libvirt network
.Pq Ql default .
.It Ev LIBVIRT_DEFAULT_URI
Default
.Ql qemu:///system ,
whoever runs it.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
0 when done; 1 on any failure, named.
.Sh EXAMPLES
Printed on a kldload desktop on 2026-09-30.
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ kvm-win --self-test
  ✔ prereqs ok (virt-install/swtpm/OVMF-secboot/zfs/default)
  ✔ OVMF: /usr/share/edk2/ovmf/OVMF_CODE.secboot.fd / VARS /usr/share/edk2/ovmf/OVMF_VARS.secboot.fd
  ✔ virtio-win URL reachable
  ✔ autounattend(win11) well-formed
  ✔ autounattend(server) well-formed

  ✔ self-test PASS
# (exited 0)
.Ed
.Pp
With a throwaway volume marked as a stopped server clone:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ kvm-win list
NAME                     OS       STATE      ZVOL
kwlist-39623             server   undefined  rpool/vms/kwlist-39623
# (exited 0)
.Ed
.Pp
What it will not destroy \(em a throwaway volume without the mark, then the
same volume marked, then a name that is not one:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
# kvm-win destroy kwtest-32679 --purge
[kvm-win] error: rpool/vms/kwtest-32679 was not made by kvm-win (no com.kldload:kvm-win); nothing destroyed
# (exited 1)
# kvm-win destroy kwtest-32679 --purge
  ✔ destroyed kwtest-32679 (zvol purged)
# (exited 0)
# kvm-win destroy ../x --purge
[kvm-win] error: not a usable VM name: '../x'
# (exited 1)
.Ed
.Pp
Building and using a golden; not run for this page, since it downloads
several gigabytes:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
# kvm-win golden win11 --iso /var/lib/libvirt/isos/Win11_24H2.iso
# kvm-win create dc01 --os server --ram 8192
# the second prints "dc01 running" once virt-install has started it
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr virt-install 1 ,
.Xr klab 8 ,
.Xr kvm-clone 8 ,
.Xr kvm-create 8 ,
.Xr zfs-clone 8
.Sh HISTORY
On 2026-09-30, writing this page:
.Cm create
destroyed any existing volume of the name it was given, and
.Cm destroy Fl -purge
destroyed any volume of any name \(em shown on a throwaway volume;
.Cm list
missed every machine whose name did not start
.Ql win- ;
and run as a user it looked at that user's own libvirt, which has no
network.
.Sh AUTHORS
.An kldload Aq Mt anthony@kldload.com
.Sh CAVEATS
A machine made before the mark existed has none;
.Cm destroy Fl -purge
leaves its volume, to be destroyed by hand.
.Pp
The evaluation editions expire; Microsoft's terms apply to what it
downloads.
